Lyric Burke was a human man of thirty-two, about five foot seven, with long brown hair he kept braided and a farmer's build. He was not born in the [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford Commune|Wrenford commune]] but joined it, having worked for one of the logging companies that tried and failed to take a foothold in the [[Verdant Expanse]]. The commune knew him as gentle and to himself. He made pottery and helped on the farmland.

He helped build the one-room house on the commune's edge and was allowed to keep it. About six months ago he went on a pilgrimage into the Verdant Expanse and did not come back. The commune left his house untouched in case he returned.

Under his pillow was a [[Phenomena/Feyrock|Feyrock]] carved into the shape of a single leaf.

Some months after he left, someone matching Lyric's description got off a train in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], walked straight to a man he had never met, spoke with him, and was never seen again. The man he met, [[People/Herald Vanderbloom|Herald Vanderbloom]], was found the next day drained to a husk in his bed.

The [[Bestiary/Fey|court of fey]] deeper in the forest said the man was not there anymore, that he was happy, and that he had not been husked. They did not know him by name.
